('Each rule acts at most once per thing per threshold — a call that breaches its SLA raises one alert at each tier, not one every five minutes. Thresholds are stored per rule, so changing “escalate after 10 minutes” to 15 needs no deployment. Every change and every manual run is written to the audit trail with your name on it.', 'st', 'Molao o mong le o mong o etsa hang feela nthong e nngwe le e nngwe moeding o mong le o mong — mohala o fetang SLA ya ona o tsosa temoso e le nngwe boemong bo bong le bo bong, eseng e le nngwe metsotso e meng le e meng e mehlano. Meedi e bolokwa ka molao o mong le o mong, kahoo ho fetola "eketsa kamora metsotso e 10" ho ya ho 15 ha ho hloke ho kenngwa. Phetoho e nngwe le e nngwe le ho etsa ho hong le ho hong ka letsoho ho ngolwa motlhaleng wa tlhahlobo le lebitso la hao.'),
('Each service''s identity — crest, colours and naming — as it appears across the platform, the responder app and printed reports.', 'st', 'Boitsebiso ba tshebeletso e nngwe le e nngwe — letshwao, mebala le mabitso — jwalo ka ha bo hlaha sethaleng sohle, ho app ya baarabi le ditlalehong tse hatisitsweng.'),
